fillPageT -- step 1 toward the first PDF (Tony, 2026-11-07, SEQ ___ R1). The top field opens one drawing context;
fill draws into it at page coordinates, for the top field and every child. The y flip and the page origin are set
once, on the top context, when makeDisplay opens it; no field below knows. A child takes the context from the top.

Rows (read in genLadder/pop.sh): FP-1 firstLight at (300,450) paints wall at its own top-left, the case that read
0,0,0,0 before. FP-2 words paints white inside its frame; FP-3 and FP-4 are just above and just below it and read
wall, so the fill stays inside. FP-5 and FP-6 are the flip by value on fpFlip: the band at the top of the form reads
lightGreen at the top of the bitmap and the bottom reads wall. The two are a pair against the same field: with the
flip removed they swap. The refusal count is read beside the child pixels: a child that refuses paints nothing.
FP-7 (rider 2 of the buy): the handed-down display is a property, so a child's list length, attributes and members, is
the same before and after makeDisplay; words and bar both carry entries, so the pair is not zero against zero.

Spellings: px and py go in through fpAt, from fpX and fpY. A top-level `field px=5 py=5;` does not take (measured 2026-11-07: pixelAt then read (0,0)).
